. 
. * We would love to test the presence of the parents/children in the household
> , searched for the SOEP relevant variable and the only relevant (which we do 
> not have) was the bfkinhh – Member of Household. In this way we cannot contro
> l for the situation if the respondents live with their children in common hou
> sehold or not *
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * 
. 
. * Our model would test whether the the proxy identified in some of the studie
> s (provided as example) would be deteremined by the controlled by the selecte
> d household and family characterstics, especially by the especially, income, 
> age, education, nationality (and origin) and marital status. We also control 
> for the survey year. 
. * The perfect dependent variable would be according to our search of the prio
> r literature and SOEP data variable from the plh set of data (https://panelda
> ta.org/soep-core/datasets/bjp/bjp_166_04) plh0395i01, plh0395i02, plh0395i03,
>  plh0395i04, plh0395i05, plh0395i06, especially "Sex assignment is not so imp
> ortant for a person’s development", which we do not have available - and we d
> o not know why *      
. * Alternatively, it would make sense to use of the proxy variables from Educa
> tional Goals (edgoal) set of variables (https://paneldata.org/soep-core/topic
> s?open=topic_edg), specifically from the qualities and abilities, such as "be
> haves like a normal girl / boy, works toward achieving his/her goals and othe
> rs. However, again this set of variables is not available in the dataset we g
> ot, so we cannot make use of those.  *    
. 
.         * Therefore, we have have to assume that having a job that requires h
> ard manual labor (plb0085) is a good measure of support for gender equality (
> hypothesis 1), 
.         * if having a job with less manual labor, the respondent is more like
> ly to support gender equality.
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with plb0085 a
> s dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as independent variabl
> e *
.         
.         
. * Correct Specification would be Logit/Probit, but the extraction and exporti
> ng code is set up to export and local OLS results, which is a reason, why we 
> decided to stay with the OLS linear model * 
.         *logit plb0085 age sex2 education_years household_income d_daughter p
